+# Deploying Aegis gRPC services (production-ready)
+
+This document explains how to build the Docker images, deploy them via the included Helm chart, and enable mTLS via Vault CSI.
+
+Build images:
+ - docker build -f ops/grpc/docker/Dockerfile.evidence -t <registry>/aegis/grpc-evidence:latest .
+ - docker build -f ops/grpc/docker/Dockerfile.dp -t <registry>/aegis/grpc-dp:latest .
+ - docker build -f ops/grpc/docker/Dockerfile.serve -t <registry>/aegis/grpc-serve:latest .
+
+Push images to your registry and update helm/aegis-grpc/values.yaml accordingly.
+
+Deploy Helm chart:
+ - helm upgrade --install aegis-grpc helm/aegis-grpc -n aegis
+
+Enable mTLS:
+ - Bootstrap Vault PKI (ops/vault/pki_bootstrap.sh)
+ - Install Vault CSI provider and configure SecretProviderClass (ops/vault/secretproviderclass-full.yaml)
+ - Deploy helm chart (certs will be mounted into /etc/certs)
+
+Notes:
+ - Docker images pre-generate protobuf stubs during build to avoid runtime codegen in production.
+ - Healthchecks use basic TCP connect probes; replace with health endpoints if you add HTTP health servers.
+ - Cert rotation must be configured in Vault and the CSI driver; see ops/vault/cert_rotation_job.yaml for a sketch.
+
